// Probe 05 — Cluster I variant: function-call result `??` "fallback"
//
// Tests the cluster I shape with a Call as the LHS.  Same parser path as
// probes 02/04: non-trivial LHS → `_ncc_N` block construction → potential
// dangling-Str escape.
//
// A Call return is more likely to involve text materialisation than a
// field read (the callee may build a fresh String via format-string ops);
// if 05 fails with the same shape as 02/04, the cluster is "any non-Var
// LHS" without an exception for call results.
//
// Expected (rustc 1.96 / macOS): FAIL on --interpret, PASS on --native.
// Pairing: 02 + 04 + 05 form the three-way LHS-shape-independence confirmation.
// Status: cluster I variant probe.

fn get_text() -> text {
  return "present";
}

fn main() {
  a = get_text() ?? "fallback";
  assert(a == "present", "probe 05: got '{a}', want 'present'");
  println("probe 05 PASSED");
}
